  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>signrank</keyword>
  <short_description>Wilcoxon signed rank test.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>p = signrank(x)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>p = signrank(x, y)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>p = signrank(x, y, Name, Value)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[p, h, stats] = signrank(...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>signrank</b> performs a paired Wilcoxon signed rank test. If <b>y</b> is omitted, values in <b>x</b> are tested against zero. If <b>y</b> is a scalar, values in <b>x</b> are tested against that scalar.</p>
    <p>Name-value arguments include <b>Alpha</b>, <b>Tail</b>, and <b>Method</b>. Zero and <b>NaN</b> differences are omitted.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[x = [1 3 5 -2];
[p, h, stats] = signrank(x)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
